# Project Professionalism

- Treat this repo as a public professional CV and portfolio site.
- Keep claims honest, especially around DevOps, infrastructure, and production experience.
- Do not invent jobs, certifications, production systems, company experience, or tool expertise.
- Prefer internship-level wording such as "learning", "academic project", "foundations", "exposure", and "seeking".
- Keep writing clear, confident, and recruiter-friendly.
- Use concise English and avoid exaggerated marketing language.
- Preserve personal contact information unless the user explicitly asks to change it.
- Before deployment changes, remember the GitHub Pages URL is expected to be `https://erionrexhepii.github.io/cv/`.
- On Windows, prefer `npm.cmd` commands in instructions because PowerShell may block `npm.ps1`.
